	<div class="text-center">
		<h1>
			Summary (1986 - Paris - Algiers - Dakar)
		</h1>
		<p>
			<img src="~/images/dakar/review/1986/1986_map.jpg" style="float: left; height: 101px" />The
			spirit of adventure and competition had long been the cornerstone of Mitsubishi
			motorsport. And nowhere was this spirit better demonstrated than at the
			Paris - Dakar rally, probably the most popular rally in the world. Since 1986
			the Pajero was the
			<img src="~/images/dakar/review/1986/1986_01.jpg" style="float: right; height: 128px" />master
			of such motorsport events, known as the most reliable and toughest machine
			in the world in such matters. Once again,
			<img src="~/images/dakar/review/1986/1986_02.jpg" style="float: left; height: 106px" />this
			insane challenge meant thundering more than 14,000 km and 22 days through the African
			desert. With three successful years behind it, the Pajero this time started
			the race as one of the favourites. The Pajero managed to confirm the previous years' successes
			with third, fifth and seventh place in the overall standings,
			and to take the marathon victory for the fourth time in a row. It was not the glory
			of the previous years, but the Pajero once again proved its ruggedness and
			its endurance and established itself as the car to beat.
		</p>
